    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d509">

                <pb facs="0799" n="778" sameAs="frus:frus1948v04/pg778"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">760D.6111/4–1648: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Minister in Finland</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Warren</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">confidential</hi>
                    </seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Helsinki</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1948-04-16T12:00:00+02:00">April 16,
                            1948—noon.</date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>244. Moscow delegates in conferring with their parties and with friends insist no
                    secret protocols to pact. Except for published preamble <pb facs="0800" n="779"
                        xml:id="pg779"/> and clause of pact no other signed documents although
                    minutes of conference made available to party leaders contain interpretations of
                    treaty clauses and are referred to by Finns as “unpublished” protocols. These
                    minutes allegedly contain only innocuous points and opposition to pact now
                    preoccupied with significance Article 2.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Warren</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
